The TypeScript adaptation computes each triangle-table entry on demand in the
same double operations instead of holding the table, runs packed and planar
input through one per-channel loop (native's two kernels compute identically),
accepts only plain decimal option values and type=t|triangular|1, refuses
type=sinusoidal (its libm sin() is not reproduced), timeline enable, and gains
past native's out_gain clipping condition (where C's double-to-integer
conversion is undefined), always writes a new owned output frame, declares the
per-channel delay rings in reserve(), enforces explicit allocation limits and
AbortSignal, and adds no FFmpeg runtime code. The original source and full
notices remain in the pinned upstream submodule.
